      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I'm defining the scope of the Python file creation for the text-to-speech task. Specifically, I need to create multiple files and ensure the \"scored\" files use an external provider, which I will need to identify in the code. I'll read and implement the `synthesize_text`.\n\n\n**Outlining File Structure**\n\nI've sketched out the initial file structure: `synthesize_text.py`, `speech_client.py`, and `speech_models.py` for helper functions. Now I'm focusing on \"scored\" files, like `synthesize_ssml.py` and `select_voice.py`, using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech. I am implementing `save_audio.py` for local file storage, with a note for future cloud storage. Further, I am starting the scaffolding for the later-step files, such as `script_translate.py` and others.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation Steps**\n\nI've outlined the core files, starting with reading `synthesize_text.py`. Next, I'll build `speech_client.py` using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech, followed by `speech_models.py` for request and response data. After that, I will tackle the \"scored\" files: `synthesize_ssml.py`, `select_voice.py`, and `save_audio.py` for local storage, before I move on to later-step files like `script_translate.py` and others.\n\n\n",
