        "text": "**Prioritizing Resource Consistency**\n\nI've determined that Azure Cognitive Services Speech should be the go-to for \"SAME-SCENARIO\" files, ensuring a unified approach within each scenario. For \"LATER-STEP\" files, I'm sticking with Google Cloud as originally planned. This separation allows for flexibility while maintaining consistency where it matters most.\n\n\n**Refining Architecture Decisions**\n\nI'm solidifying the architecture. Azure Cognitive Services Speech will handle \"SAME-SCENARIO\" files, aligning with `synthesize_text.py`. I'm committed to Google Cloud for \"LATER-STEP\" files. I've broken the work down into clear implementation steps, including `speech_client.py` and `speech_models.py` for Azure. I've also planned the implementation of various scripts, including those for translation, safety checks, and embeddings on the Google Cloud side.\n\n\n**Confirming Service Implementation**\n\nNow I'm completely sure that `synthesize_text.py` uses Azure Cognitive Services Speech. Because of this, \"SAME-SCENARIO\" files will also be generated with Azure. I've broken the architecture into clear actionables. Implementing `speech_client.py` and `speech_models.py` will be first on the Azure side, and then I will move on to the Google Cloud scripts.\n\n\n",
